{"id":"u-1065cb7a-0a90-422b-870d-268cf59044a8","src":"community","title":"The King Engine (3 days)","author":"Jaron Z.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/the-king-engine","desc":"3 day per week, upper body focused program. Decent amout of volume with high intensity.\n\nMy recommended training time line:\nDay 1 (Upper 1)\nDay 2 Off or Lower\nDay 3 Off or Lower\nDay 4 Off, Lower, or Upper 2 (if recovered)\nDay 5 Off or Upper 2 (if you needed an extra day for recovery)\nDay 6 Off\nDay 7 Off\n\nSince this is a 3 day split, it's fairly flexible, but it is important to do Upper 2 on day 4 or 5 if you want to train on the same days every week.\n\n-Don't worry about trying to hit the top end of the rep ranges, just make sure your reps don't fall below the minimum rep range. \n\n-There should be some rep dropoff set to set. If your reps don't drop from the 1st set vs the last set, you're not training close enough to failure.\n\n-Each week try to add 5-10 pounds to compound lifts (2.5 pounds for isolations) and match reps from the previous week's session. OR beat your reps by 1 from the previous week's session, with the same weight from the previous week.\n\n-Note: *The first set of each exercise is the one you're trying to match/beat reps from the previous week. This is how you're going to gauge performance. \nMatching subsequent sets isn't as important, although performance should be similar to the previous week's session.*\n\n-If you're unable to match, or beat reps, stick with the same weight next week, until you can beat your reps; then repeat.\n\n\n*How to perform a Myo rep match set*\n\n-Perform the 1st set as usual. This 1st set should be taken to the appropriate RPE. \n\n-On all subsequent sets hit the same amount of reps as your first set, with as many rest pause, mini sets as it takes. \n\n-Rest a normal amount of time in between each myo rep match set.","level":["Beginner","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Women's"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":3,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-05-23T20:18:33.392Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Upper 1 'Arms Mode'","Lower 'Cue the King Engine'","Upper 2 'The Ultimate Attack'"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Extension (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":4}],"note":"Perform overhead"},{"n":"Bicep Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Lateral Raise","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":4}]},{"n":"Incline Chest Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Fly (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Row (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":4}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"High Bar Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":4}]},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":20,"rpe":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Leg Press Calf Raise","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":10,"x":5}]},{"n":"Cable Crunch","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hanging Leg Raise","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Guillotine Press","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}],"note":"*Or Flat Dumbell Press"},{"n":"Low to high Cable Flye","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":4}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":4}],"note":"Myo rep match sets after set 1"},{"n":"Bicep Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":4}],"note":"Myo rep match sets after set 1"},{"n":"Overhead Tricep Extension (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"rpeH